{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md | sed -n '154,182p;235,284p;570,588p' && rg -n -i 'joint|separate|P-v4|P-v8|reconcil' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{BLIND-RESULT,BLIND2-RESULT,BLIND3-RESULT,RESULT}.md\"","aggregated_output":"   154\t**Value × reader.**\n   155\t- `from_answer`'s output is read by `check`, `publish_decision`, `merge`, `card_view` and `normalise`. It uses the internal names\n   156\t  those readers read (`evidence`, `inputs`, `rests_on`, `outcome`, `reference`), and the dropped keys never appear.\n   157\t- `merge`'s unification of a shared forecast uses `evaluate`'s values with no bound.\n   158\t- The reader brief is unchanged. Its `deciding_gap` question is where readers judge the recorded conversions and estimates.\n   159\t\n   160\t**State × event:** unchanged from D731. A refusal is retried once, diagnostic only; the first attempt is scored.\n   161\t\n   162\t## 5. The $0 blind test (registered; REPAIR-DESIGN.md §5 with rounds 51's fixes)\n   163\t\n   164\t**Inputs.** Each case's archive, call, question, ladder and unit are registered, and the build refuses a heading that differs.\n   165\t\n   166\t| Case | Archive / call | Key | Ladder edges ($bn) | Role |\n   167\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n   168\t| P (joint), P-v4, P-v8 (separate) | old-1 v4 8810, v8 8816 | NVIDIA revenue company FY2027; NVIDIA revenue Data Center FY2027 | 431.2/392/352.8/313.6; 400/350/300/250 | the pair; 79 quotes absent from the gate |\n   169\t| S | old-3 v6 9043 | four largest AI hyperscalers, data-center capex, combined, CY2026 | 500/600/700/800 | fresh: 41 of 50 quotes absent from the gate |\n   170\t| O | old-2 v29 8507 | NVIDIA equity investment commitments company end of FY2027 (the fiscal year-end balance the annual report publishes) | 25/50/75/100 | control |\n   171\t| E | old-3 v41 9071 | NVIDIA revenue Vera CPU FY2028 | 50/40/30/20 | control |\n   172\t\n   173\t**Part A, code, $0.** Each case asserts its intended rule and message. The schema's validity is checked first, so a schema error\n   174\tcannot mask the rule under test.\n   175\t- **A1, correct forms.** Each passes:\n   176\t  - a $4.5 billion ± 3% guidance as two sources with apply_growth ends;\n   177\t  - Q1 + Q2 = H1;\n   178\t  - FY − Q1-Q3 = Q4;\n   179\t  - a year-over-year rate on last year's quarter (recorded);\n   180\t  - whole × mix through share;\n   181\t  - \"over $300 billion\" with qualifier over;\n   182\t  - \"-3%\";\n   235\t  - a figure id equal to a passage id (S7);\n   236\t  - \"plus or minus 2%\" copied as \"2%\" and used as +2% for the range (S1);\n   237\t  - a euro amount (S1).\n   238\t- **A3:** each mistake must be refused by the schema or **actually refused** by its stated rule (asserted). \"first half\" is refused by\n   239\t  S8 when summed. \"1.05 USD trillion\" fails the schema, and \"1050 USD bn\" passes.\n   240\t- **A4, the end to end rehearsal.** One v13s reply goes through the first attempt, the separate-arm reconciliation, the card render and\n   241\t  recovery. For each named defect, the defective answer fails its rule while its paired correct answer reaches the reader's card. The\n   242\t  old run's `results.json` reproduces from its journals with the ledger snapshot saved inside it.\n   243\t\n   244\t**[52] Readers.**\n   245\t- **What they get.** Both readers get the same complete shown passages, with the writer's identity and the checker's decision masked.\n   246\t- **What they mark, on every first reply:**\n   247\t  - whether each forecast is supported, naming the passage or assumption that puts it in its band;\n   248\t  - any of D737's five defects;\n   249\t  - broken structure.\n   250\t- **The wording review is separate.** Refusals are revealed only after that marking, for the review of whether the request states\n   251\t  the rule.\n   252\t- **An accepted reply with a named defect** (marked by both readers, or by the third reader) is a stop.\n   253\t- **INCOMPLETE** is judged against the inventory of 12 first replies and 24 readings plus the third readings due.\n   254\t\n   255\t**Part B, blind writers ($0 at the provider).**\n   256\t- **The writers.** Each of the six cases is written once by a fresh Claude subagent and once by a fresh read-only Codex session, 12\n   257\t  sessions in all. Each gets only that case's exact outgoing system text, user text and schema.\n   258\t- **The first outputs** go through `model.check_schema`, `from_answer` and `check` unedited.\n   259\t- **The readers.** Two readers who wrote neither the design nor the answers (a Claude subagent and a Codex session) grade **every**\n   260\t  answer, accepted or refused, against the shown passages. For each answer they record:\n   261\t  - for each refusal, whether the exact request states the condition (the sentence quoted) and whether the answer was right;\n   262\t  - for each accepted answer, whether each forecast is supported, and whether its recorded conversions or estimates decide its band.\n   263\t- **A third reader** settles disagreements.\n   264\t- **Usable** means accepted, publishable by `publish_decision`, and supported by the readers. For the joint case, both forecasts must\n   265\t  be supported in one reply.\n   266\t\n   267\t**Stop.** The test stops on any of these:\n   268\t- an A1 form refused;\n   269\t- an A2 defect not refused by its rule;\n   270\t- an A3 mistake neither impossible nor stated;\n   271\t- a Part B refusal whose condition the request does not state, or that refuses a right answer;\n   272\t- an INCOMPLETE run;\n   273\t- a case with zero usable first replies across both writers;\n   274\t- the joint case without both supported forecasts in one reply.\n   275\t\n   276\t**A clean result** goes to Alex as the request for the paid re-send: the same 36 requests rebuilt in v13s, under a new decision with\n   277\tD725's lines. Only that run measures whether luna can do it.\n   278\t\n   279\t**[D742] Registered before the third run (council rounds 56–56c).** The re-run stopped on one S4 refusal of a sound answer\n   280\t(`BLIND2-RESULT.md`). The cause was the request: the system text said to carry \"the guided growth forward\", while the schema allowed a\n   281\tguidance rate only as \"a stated benchmark for an estimate\" and the header required every path to go through the forecast. S4 is\n   282\tunchanged (rounds 56 and 56b showed that both a blanket and a narrowed exemption let a reset to guidance publish). The request now states\n   283\tone rule in the system text, the schema and the header: guidance informs the pace; the forecast pace is recorded as an estimate that\n   284\tnames its benchmark in `rests_on`; the quarter's dollar value is the one forecast figure. The rules for the third run:\n   570\t  - it leaves the $37B answer a boundary case;\n   571\t  - the explained near-cutoff S forecasts stand.\n   572\t  - Council 68 replaced \"across the plausible readings\" with \"weigh the plausible alternatives … whether the evidence as a whole favours\n   573\t    one band\". The first wording could read as requiring a forecast to survive every reading, which is stricter than D747.\n   574\t- **Design and tally.** D750's, unchanged (`blind7.py` wraps `blind5.py`), on a new run folder,\n   575\t  `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind7-2026-11-23/`:\n   576\t  - S, E and P-v8, each with one fresh Claude and one fresh read-only Codex writer;\n   577\t  - the same two controls, each with its original request;\n   578\t  - fresh readers of both families, with adjudication where they disagree;\n   579\t  - the decisive premise and its passage support recorded for every settled S and E vote (council 66).\n   580\t- **Exit rule (council 67):**\n   581\t  - a clean pass goes to Alex for the paid authorization;\n   582\t  - a settled failure or a persistent split ends this wording loop, and the publication choice for E-type cases returns to Alex.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RESULT.md:28:- **Disjoint inputs:** old-2's two questions share 106 of about 1,300 linked evidence items. Their 09-20 requests share 5 entries and\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RESULT.md:43:2. **Related questions compute shared quantities separately.** The judging unit is one question, with 0 dependencies in 139\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RESULT.md:67:- **When figures cannot be reconciled, the forecast shows as unresolved,** not as two incompatible answers.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RESULT.md:87:  - **The arms:** the 09-20 total and Data Center pair in each draw, three samples each, judged jointly and separately under the same\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RESULT.md:90:  - **Pass:** the joint arm publishes both answers usable and source-supported in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot,\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RESULT.md:91:    and at least 3 more usable pairs than the separate arm. Zero published hard contradictions, internal-as-market references, or\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:17:- **Every case has a usable reply.** The joint case has both forecasts supported in one reply (R02 and R11).\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:28:| P (joint) | v4 416.3, v8 386.1, both rung 2 | v4 420.9, v8 391.0, both rung 2 |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:29:| P-v4 | 419.3, rung 2 | 416.3, rung 2 |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:30:| P-v8 | 387.4, rung 2 | 388.1, rung 2 |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:81:  - C-disjoint was marked broken structure by both readers.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:84:- **STOP again, as written: Q10 (P-v8, Codex writer).**\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:107:  - All five controls passed: K-midpoint was not marked; K-misread was marked by both readers; K-overlap was not marked; K-disjoint was\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:133:  | P-v4 | both writers |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:134:  | P-v8 | both writers |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND-RESULT.md:6:2. An accepted reply carries a named defect. P-v4's Codex writer used two values for company Q3 revenue: the $108B guidance to set a\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND-RESULT.md:23:| P (joint) | publish: v4 416.3, v8 384.9, both rung 2 | publish: v4 417.4, v8 386.5, both rung 2 |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND-RESULT.md:24:| P-v4 | publish: 417.4, rung 2 | publish: 419.8, rung 2 |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND-RESULT.md:25:| P-v8 | publish: 385.9, rung 2 | publish: 387.1, rung 2 |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND-RESULT.md:44:- **R06 (P-v4, Codex writer), two forecasts of one quarter.** Both readers and both adjudicators marked it.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND-RESULT.md:87:- **The joint and separate answers in P agree closely.** v4 is 416–420 and v8 385–387, all rung 2. This is one draw each, a strong\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND-RESULT.md:88:  writer, and not gpt-6-luna. It is no evidence for D725's joint-versus-separate question.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND-RESULT.md:92:- **STOP is correct as registered**, and every count reconciles. Three wordings above are corrected.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND2-RESULT.md:4:- P-v4's Claude writer was refused by S4: \"v4: uses F4 for NVIDIA | revenue | company | FY2027 Q3 beside its forecast figure F8\".\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND2-RESULT.md:14:- Every case has at least one usable reply. The joint case has both forecasts supported in one reply (R05 and R09).\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND2-RESULT.md:17:  marks were jointly rejected, nine split and none was jointly upheld (Council round 56).\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND2-RESULT.md:27:| P (joint) | publish: v4 413.1, v8 382.4, both rung 2 | publish: v4 419.2, v8 388.3, both rung 2 |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND2-RESULT.md:28:| P-v4 | **refused (S4)**: 416.6, rung 2 | publish: 416.4, rung 2 |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND2-RESULT.md:29:| P-v8 | publish: 383.6, rung 2 | publish: 388.6, rung 2 |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"**A. Keep the paid comparison on hold because Alex chose a clean free test as the condition for spending again.** In the last test, both readers rejected the $37B sales forecast because no source supported the 85% growth rate that produced it. [DECISIONS-log.md:11645](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11645) · [BLIND7-RESULT.md:19](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND7-RESULT.md:19)\n\n1. **What the free tests measured.** The later tests used only the Data Center forecast from the pair. Earlier free tests did ask for company and Data Center revenue both together and separately. Claude’s narrower point holds: only the paid comparison can establish whether Luna produces more usable pairs when it calculates them together. [BLIND-RESULT.md:23](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND-RESULT.md:23) · [SMALL-DESIGN.md:576](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:576) · [PAID-GATE.md:270](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:270)\n\n2. **What failed.** “Claude failed five times” overstates the record. None of its five sales forecasts earned settled support, but the $42B answer split readers. Codex also invented cuts twice before giving three accepted “can’t tell” answers on the same passages. Readers still disagreed on a separate spending forecast. Luna’s behavior remains unknown. Claude is right that a completed paid run scores STOP if readers find that an unsupported adjustment decided a published standalone forecast. [BLIND6-RESULT.md:40](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND6-RESULT.md:40) · [BLIND7-RESULT.md:30](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND7-RESULT.md:30) · [PAID-GATE.md:267](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:267)\n\n3. **Cost.** The figures hold. Alex authorized $0.50 for one earlier run, which spent $0.3677 including retries. B would require fresh authorization for up to $0.50 total. [DECISIONS-log.md:11117](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11117) · [PAID-GATE-RESULT.md:10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE-RESULT.md:10)\n\n4. **Production.** B is the remaining registered test that could earn a production design. A also gives Alex a first-release outcome he expressly accepted: readers see the question, its sources and “Forecast unavailable.” His later direction to converge kept paid work on hold. [PAID-GATE.md:278](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:278) · [DECISIONS-log.md:11004](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11004) · [DECISIONS-log.md:11658](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11658)\n\n5. **How far the diagnosis reaches.** The last test located one clear failure. Repeating the same passages leaves its frequency elsewhere unknown. Question 1 settles what readers should see, and the final test shows a writer can still give them an unsupported number under that instruction. [BLIND7-RESULT.md:19](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND7-RESULT.md:19) · [BLIND7-RESULT.md:30](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND7-RESULT.md:30)\n\n**Yes, present B as the alternative.** Its strongest case is that a one-time exception would buy a direct answer from Luna on a question the free tests could not settle. Tell Alex that 36 scored requests and any diagnostic retries share the $0.50 cap, and that a pass earns design work only. [PAID-GATE.md:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:20) · [PAID-GATE.md:37](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:37) · [PAID-GATE.md:280](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:280)"}}
